<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">
  <diagram name="Word Processor LLD" id="wordprocessor">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1434" dy="844" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1920" pageHeight="1300">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        
        <!-- Title -->
        <mxCell id="title" value="WORD PROCESSOR - Flyweight Design Pattern (Memory Optimization via Data Sharing)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=20;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="1840" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- SECTION 1-3: CLASS DIAGRAM -->
        <mxCell id="subtitle1" value="SECTION 1-3: CLASS DIAGRAM (Flyweight Pattern - Intrinsic vs Extrinsic Data)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="70" width="1000" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="iletter_interface" value="&lt;&lt;interface&gt;&gt;&#xa;ILetter&#xa;&#xa;+ display(row, col): void&#xa;  // row, col = extrinsic data" style="swimlane;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="120" width="260" height="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="documentcharacter_class" value="DocumentCharacter&#xa;(implements ILetter)&#xa;&#xa;INTRINSIC DATA (shared):&#xa;- character: char  // 't', 'h', 'i', 's'&#xa;- fontType: String  // 'Arial'&#xa;- fontSize: int     // 10&#xa;&#xa;+ DocumentCharacter(char, font, size)&#xa;  // Constructor sets intrinsic data&#xa;  // IMMUTABLE (private final, no setters!)&#xa;&#xa;+ display(row, col): void&#xa;  // Uses intrinsic + extrinsic&#xa;  // Render character at (row, col)&#xa;  // with fontType &amp; fontSize" style="swimlane;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="340" y="120" width="360" height="280" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="letterfactory_class" value="LetterFactory (Singleton)&#xa;&#xa;CACHING:&#xa;- characterCache:&#xa;    Map&lt;Character, ILetter&gt;&#xa;  // Key: 't', 'h', 'i', etc.&#xa;  // Value: DocumentCharacter instance&#xa;&#xa;+ createLetter(char): ILetter&#xa;  if (cache.containsKey(char)):&#xa;    return cache.get(char)  // REUSE!&#xa;  else:&#xa;    letter = new DocumentCharacter(&#xa;      char, 'Arial', 10)&#xa;    cache.put(char, letter)&#xa;    return letter" style="swimlane;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="740" y="120" width="380" height="280" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- Flyweight Pattern Explanation -->
        <mxCell id="pattern_explanation" value="FLYWEIGHT PATTERN STRUCTURE:&#xa;&#xa;PROBLEM: Memory Exhaustion&#xa;Document: 'This is the data we want to write'&#xa;Total characters: 58&#xa;&#xa;WITHOUT FLYWEIGHT:&#xa;- Create 58 DocumentCharacter objects&#xa;- Each object stores: char, fontType, fontSize, row, col&#xa;- 't' appears 7 times → 7 separate objects for 't'&#xa;- All 7 look identical (same font, size) except position&#xa;- Memory waste: 7 × sizeof(DocumentCharacter)&#xa;&#xa;For 1 million characters: 1M objects created!&#xa;If each object = 50 bytes → 50MB wasted&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;WITH FLYWEIGHT:&#xa;- Identify INTRINSIC data (shared among objects):&#xa;  • character, fontType, fontSize → SAME for all 't's&#xa;- Identify EXTRINSIC data (differs per object):&#xa;  • row, col → DIFFERENT for each 't' position&#xa;&#xa;- Create DocumentCharacter with ONLY intrinsic data&#xa;- Pass extrinsic data (row, col) to display() method&#xa;- Cache objects by character in LetterFactory&#xa;&#xa;For 'ttttttt' (7 't's):&#xa;- 1 DocumentCharacter object created for 't'&#xa;- Shared by all 7 positions&#xa;- display(0,0), display(0,5), display(0,10), etc.&#xa;- Memory: 1 object instead of 7&#xa;&#xa;For 1 million characters with ~100 unique chars:&#xa;- 100 objects created (instead of 1M)&#xa;- 99.99% memory saved!&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;KEY REQUIREMENTS FOR FLYWEIGHT:&#xa;&#xa;1. MEMORY IS LIMITED&#xa;   - Interviewer says: 'We have only 2GB RAM'&#xa;   - Without flyweight: objects consume 5GB → CRASH&#xa;&#xa;2. OBJECTS SHARE DATA&#xa;   - Multiple objects have common properties&#xa;   - Example: 1000 'A's look identical (font, size same)&#xa;&#xa;3. OBJECT CREATION IS EXPENSIVE&#xa;   - 2D Sprite bitmap array (game graphics) → heavy&#xa;   - Loading font rendering data → slow&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;INTRINSIC vs EXTRINSIC DATA:&#xa;&#xa;INTRINSIC (invariant, shared):&#xa;- Data that DOESN'T change per object&#xa;- Same for ALL instances of a type&#xa;- Example: All 't's have same font='Arial', size=10&#xa;- Stored INSIDE flyweight object&#xa;- Immutable (private final, no setters)&#xa;&#xa;EXTRINSIC (variant, context-dependent):&#xa;- Data that CHANGES per object&#xa;- Unique to each instance&#xa;- Example: Each 't' at different (row, col) position&#xa;- Passed as METHOD PARAMETER to flyweight&#xa;- NOT stored in flyweight object&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;IMMUTABILITY REQUIREMENT:&#xa;- Flyweight object MUST be immutable&#xa;- Why? Shared by multiple contexts&#xa;- If mutable: changing one affects all sharers!&#xa;- How? private final fields, NO setters, only getters&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;CACHING MECHANISM:&#xa;- Factory pattern with Map&lt;Key, Flyweight&gt;&#xa;- Key = intrinsic data identifier (character)&#xa;- Before creating new object: check cache&#xa;- If exists: return cached (REUSE)&#xa;- If not exists: create, cache, return&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;FLYWEIGHT vs SINGLETON:&#xa;SINGLETON: ONE instance for entire application&#xa;FLYWEIGHT: ONE instance PER intrinsic state combination&#xa;Example: One 't' object, one 'h' object, one 'i' object" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=10;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="460" width="1080" height="900" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- Example Flow -->
        <mxCell id="example_title" value="EXAMPLE: TEXT EDITOR FLOW" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1160" y="120" width="720" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="example_flow" value="TYPING 'this is the data':&#xa;&#xa;User types: t-h-i-s (space) i-s (space) t-h-e (space) d-a-t-a&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;CHARACTER 1: 't' at (0, 0)&#xa;LetterFactory.createLetter('t')&#xa;  → cache.containsKey('t')? NO&#xa;  → new DocumentCharacter('t', 'Arial', 10)&#xa;  → cache.put('t', tObject)&#xa;  → return tObject&#xa;tObject.display(0, 0)&#xa;  → Render 't' at row=0, col=0 using Arial, size 10&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;CHARACTER 2: 'h' at (0, 1)&#xa;LetterFactory.createLetter('h')&#xa;  → cache.containsKey('h')? NO&#xa;  → new DocumentCharacter('h', 'Arial', 10)&#xa;  → cache.put('h', hObject)&#xa;  → return hObject&#xa;hObject.display(0, 1)&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;CHARACTER 3: 'i' at (0, 2)&#xa;[Similar: create iObject, cache, display]&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;CHARACTER 4: 's' at (0, 3)&#xa;[Similar: create sObject, cache, display]&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;CHARACTER 5: ' ' (space) at (0, 4)&#xa;[Create spaceObject, cache, display]&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;CHARACTER 6: 'i' at (0, 5)  ← REUSE!&#xa;LetterFactory.createLetter('i')&#xa;  → cache.containsKey('i')? YES&#xa;  → return cache.get('i')  // SAME iObject from index 2!&#xa;iObject.display(0, 5)  // Different row, col (extrinsic)&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;CHARACTER 7: 's' at (0, 6)  ← REUSE!&#xa;LetterFactory.createLetter('s')&#xa;  → cache.containsKey('s')? YES&#xa;  → return sObject  // SAME sObject from index 3!&#xa;sObject.display(0, 6)&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;CHARACTER 10: 't' at (0, 9)  ← REUSE!&#xa;LetterFactory.createLetter('t')&#xa;  → cache.containsKey('t')? YES&#xa;  → return tObject  // SAME tObject from index 0!&#xa;tObject.display(0, 9)&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;MEMORY ANALYSIS:&#xa;'this is the data' = 17 characters (without spaces counted separately)&#xa;Unique characters: t, h, i, s, e, d, a (7 unique)&#xa;&#xa;WITHOUT FLYWEIGHT:&#xa;- 17 DocumentCharacter objects&#xa;- Each object ~50 bytes&#xa;- Total: 17 × 50 = 850 bytes&#xa;&#xa;WITH FLYWEIGHT:&#xa;- 7 DocumentCharacter objects (for 7 unique chars)&#xa;- 7 × 50 = 350 bytes&#xa;- Savings: (850 - 350) / 850 = 58.8%&#xa;&#xa;For 10,000 characters (typical document):&#xa;Unique chars: ~50 (lowercase, uppercase, digits, punctuation)&#xa;WITHOUT: 10,000 × 50 = 500,000 bytes (488 KB)&#xa;WITH: 50 × 50 = 2,500 bytes (2.4 KB)&#xa;Savings: 99.5%!&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;CODE STRUCTURE:&#xa;&#xa;class Editor {&#xa;  List&lt;ILetter&gt; letters;  // Store flyweight references&#xa;  List&lt;Position&gt; positions;  // Store extrinsic data separately&#xa;  &#xa;  void typeCharacter(char c, int row, int col) {&#xa;    ILetter letter = LetterFactory.createLetter(c);&#xa;    letters.add(letter);&#xa;    positions.add(new Position(row, col));&#xa;  }&#xa;  &#xa;  void render() {&#xa;    for (int i = 0; i < letters.size(); i++) {&#xa;      Position pos = positions.get(i);&#xa;      letters.get(i).display(pos.row, pos.col);&#xa;    }&#xa;  }&#xa;}&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;IMMUTABILITY ENFORCEMENT:&#xa;&#xa;class DocumentCharacter implements ILetter {&#xa;  private final char character;  // final = immutable&#xa;  private final String fontType;&#xa;  private final int fontSize;&#xa;  &#xa;  // Constructor ONLY way to set values&#xa;  public DocumentCharacter(char c, String font, int size) {&#xa;    this.character = c;&#xa;    this.fontType = font;&#xa;    this.fontSize = size;&#xa;  }&#xa;  &#xa;  // ONLY getters, NO setters&#xa;  public char getCharacter() { return character; }&#xa;  public String getFontType() { return fontType; }&#xa;  public int getFontSize() { return fontSize; }&#xa;  &#xa;  // Extrinsic data passed as parameters&#xa;  public void display(int row, int col) {&#xa;    System.out.println('Render ' + character +&#xa;      ' at (' + row + ',' + col + ')' +&#xa;      ' font=' + fontType + ' size=' + fontSize);&#xa;  }&#xa;}&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;FACTORY CACHING:&#xa;&#xa;class LetterFactory {&#xa;  private static Map&lt;Character, ILetter&gt; cache = new HashMap<>();&#xa;  &#xa;  public static ILetter createLetter(char c) {&#xa;    if (cache.containsKey(c)) {&#xa;      System.out.println('Reusing flyweight for: ' + c);&#xa;      return cache.get(c);&#xa;    } else {&#xa;      System.out.println('Creating new flyweight for: ' + c);&#xa;      ILetter letter = new DocumentCharacter(c, 'Arial', 10);&#xa;      cache.put(c, letter);&#xa;      return letter;&#xa;    }&#xa;  }&#xa;}&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;ALTERNATIVE USE CASE: GAME SPRITES&#xa;&#xa;Problem: 5 lakh humanoid robots, 5 lakh robotic dogs&#xa;Each robot: x, y, type, sprite (2D bitmap)&#xa;Sprite = 30KB each&#xa;Total: 10 lakh × 30KB = 30GB!  (RAM = 16GB) → CRASH&#xa;&#xa;Solution:&#xa;INTRINSIC: sprite (same for all humanoids), type&#xa;EXTRINSIC: x, y (position)&#xa;&#xa;class Robot {&#xa;  // EXTRINSIC (not stored)&#xa;  // x, y passed to display()&#xa;}&#xa;&#xa;class RobotType {  // FLYWEIGHT&#xa;  private final Sprite sprite;  // INTRINSIC (30KB)&#xa;  private final String type;&#xa;  &#xa;  void display(int x, int y) {&#xa;    renderSprite(sprite, x, y);&#xa;  }&#xa;}&#xa;&#xa;RobotFactory caches 2 objects:&#xa;- humanoidType (sprite for humanoid)&#xa;- dogType (sprite for dog)&#xa;&#xa;Memory: 2 × 30KB = 60KB (instead of 30GB)&#xa;Savings: 99.9998%!" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=9;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1160" y="160" width="720" height="1200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- SECTION 4: ER DIAGRAM -->
        <mxCell id="title_er" value="SECTION 4: ER DIAGRAM" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1400" width="1080" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="er_character" value="Character (Flyweight Pool)&#xa;&#xa;PK  characterId: INT&#xa;    char: CHAR(1)  // 't', 'h', etc.&#xa;    fontType: VARCHAR(50)&#xa;    fontSize: INT" style="swimlane;fontStyle=1;align=left;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1460" width="240" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="er_document" value="Document&#xa;&#xa;PK  documentId: INT&#xa;    documentName: VARCHAR(200)&#xa;    createdAt: DATETIME" style="swimlane;fontStyle=1;align=left;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="320" y="1460" width="240" height="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="er_documentchar" value="DocumentCharacterInstance&#xa;&#xa;PK  instanceId: INT&#xa;FK  documentId: INT&#xa;FK  characterId: INT  // Flyweight ref&#xa;    row: INT  // Extrinsic data&#xa;    col: INT  // Extrinsic data&#xa;    sequence: INT" style="swimlane;fontStyle=1;align=left;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="600" y="1460" width="280" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- SECTION 7: SCENARIO QUESTIONS -->
        <mxCell id="title_scenario" value="SECTION 7: SCENARIO QUESTIONS" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1660" width="1080" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="scenario" value="Q1: User changes font size mid-document ('Arial 10' → 'Arial 12'). Flyweight pattern breaks?&#xa;A1: Font attributes ARE intrinsic (shared). Solution: Create NEW flyweight pool for 'Arial 12'. Factory key becomes (char, font, size). Example: cache key = 't_Arial_10' vs 't_Arial_12'. Multiple flyweights per character, differentiated by formatting. Trade-off: more flyweights, but still shared across same formatting.&#xa;&#xa;Q2: Flyweight pattern vs Prototype pattern? Both seem to reuse objects.&#xa;A2: FLYWEIGHT: Share ONE object across multiple contexts (same 't' instance used 100 times). Zero cloning. Immutable shared state. PROTOTYPE: CLONE object for each use (copy 't' object 100 times). Each context gets separate instance. Mutable independent copies. Intent differs: Flyweight = memory saving via sharing, Prototype = object creation via copying.&#xa;&#xa;Q3: How to handle undo/redo with Flyweight? Typing 'hello', undo to 'hell', redo to 'hello'.&#xa;A3: Store extrinsic data (positions) in separate undo stack. Undo: pop last position from document.positions list (flyweight reference remains in factory cache, just not used). Redo: re-add position. Flyweight objects never deleted from cache (persistent for document lifetime). Undo/redo operates on document structure, not flyweight pool.&#xa;&#xa;Q4: Memory limited to 100MB, document has 10 million characters. Still not enough?&#xa;A4: Two-tier flyweight: (1) Character flyweight (100 objects cached). (2) String flyweight for repeated words/phrases ('the', 'and' appear thousands of times → store as single string, reference by ID). Run-length encoding for repeated chars ('tttttt' → {char: 't', count: 6}). Lazy loading: cache only visible viewport characters, evict off-screen (LRU cache).&#xa;&#xa;Q5: When NOT to use Flyweight Pattern?&#xa;A5: DON'T use if: (1) Objects don't share significant data (each object unique → no intrinsic state). (2) Memory not a concern (premature optimization). (3) Object creation cheap (no heavy sprites/bitmaps). (4) Few object instances (10 objects → flyweight overhead not worth it). (5) Extrinsic data dominates (small intrinsic, large extrinsic → little savings)." style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=10;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1720" width="1080" height="520" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
